# Code Conventions & Standards

Strict TypeScript typing, Next.js 16 App Router conventions, explicit component boundaries, and clean separation of concerns across the marketing site.

## Invariant Rules

- **No `any` or `unknown`** — 100% explicit TypeScript typing across props, params, returns, and state.
- **Async `params` unwrapping** — In Next.js 15+, page and layout `params` / `searchParams` are Promises; ALWAYS `await params` before accessing properties.
- **`setRequestLocale(locale)` on every server route** — Call `setRequestLocale(locale)` at the top of every localized page and layout for cached static rendering.
- **Server components by default** — Mark files with `'use client'` ONLY when they need local state, DOM/canvas APIs, event listeners, or client-side analytics.
- **Locale-aware navigation** — ALWAYS import `Link`, `useRouter`, and `usePathname` from `@/i18n/navigation`, NEVER bare `next/link` on localized pages.
- **No direct `localStorage` without sync** — Use `@/lib/utils/cross-app-sync` to ensure theme and locale sync across `.cash-vio.com` subdomains.

## ❌ FORBIDDEN vs ✅ REQUIRED

### 1. Component Boundaries & Translations

```tsx
// ❌ FORBIDDEN — Unnecessary 'use client' for display-only translated section
'use client';
import { useTranslations } from 'next-intl';

export function FeatureCard({ name }: { name: string }) {
  const t = useTranslations('features');
  return <div className="p-4">{t(name)}</div>;
}

// ✅ REQUIRED — Server component with pre-translated props or async server translations
import { getTranslations } from 'next-intl/server';
import { type Locale } from '@/i18n/routing';

interface FeatureCardProps {
  title: string;
  description: string;
}

export function FeatureCard({ title, description }: FeatureCardProps) {
  return (
    <div className="p-4">
      <h3>{title}</h3>
      <p>{description}</p>
    </div>
  );
}
```

### 2. Async Params & Static Locale Setup

```tsx
// ❌ FORBIDDEN — Synchronous params access without setRequestLocale
export default function Page({ params }: { params: { locale: string } }) {
  const locale = params.locale; // Crashes in Next.js 15+
  return <div>{locale}</div>;
}

// ✅ REQUIRED — Awaited params + setRequestLocale
import { setRequestLocale } from 'next-intl/server';
import { type Locale } from '@/i18n/routing';

interface Props {
  params: Promise<{ locale: string }>;
}

export default async function Page({ params }: Props) {
  const { locale } = await params;
  setRequestLocale(locale);
  const typedLocale = locale as Locale;

  return <div>{typedLocale}</div>;
}
```

### 3. Navigation Links

```tsx
// ❌ FORBIDDEN — Bare next/link losing locale prefix or requiring manual prefixing
import Link from 'next/link';

<Link href={locale === 'en' ? '/features' : '/ar/features'}>Features</Link>

// ✅ REQUIRED — Locale-aware Link from @/i18n/navigation
import { Link } from '@/i18n/navigation';

<Link href="/features">Features</Link>
```

## Naming Conventions

| Target | Convention | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Components | PascalCase | `LedgerHero.tsx`, `ReceiptCard.tsx` |
| Component Props | PascalCase with `Props` suffix | `LedgerHeroProps`, `ButtonProps` |
| Functions & methods | camelCase, verb-first | `buildPageMetadata`, `formatNumber` |
| Hook functions | camelCase with `use` prefix | `useLocaleConfig`, `useTranslations` |
| Files & directories | kebab-case | `barcode-generator-tool.tsx`, `feature-landing-shell.tsx` |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `SCROLL_DEPTH_MILESTONES`, `COOKIE_KEYS` |
| CSS variables | kebab-case with `--` prefix | `--ledger-line`, `--font-receipt` |
| Translation namespaces | camelCase | `freePos`, `marginCalculator`, `metadata` |

## Code Organization

- Reusable UI primitives live in `src/components/ui/` (buttons, inputs, cards, badges).
- Marketing domain sections live in `src/components/marketing/` (ledger components, receipts, comparisons, FAQs).
- Global layout components live in `src/components/layout/` (header, footer, nav drawers, theme/locale switchers).
- Complex feature domains live in `src/features/<domain>/` (tools, industries, order-export).
- Configuration & constants live in `src/config/` (`seo.ts`, `env.ts`, `navigation.ts`).
